label Greeting
# [signal arg="refresh_desires"]
if {Transaction_Chapter} == 0:
	Brahim: Magandang araw. [pause=0.3] You must be the new face behind the counter. I'm Brahim.
	Brahim: I just moved back home to Karimlan a few weeks ago. Left my corporate job in the city—couldn't stare at another spreadsheet under fluorescent lights.
	- That's a big change of pace.
		Brahim: The best kind. Out here I'm apprenticing under my father—he's been Karimlan's albularyo for forty years.
	- How's the quiet life treating you?
		Brahim: Honestly? I slept eight straight hours for the first time in years. My father's been teaching me the old albularyo craft since I got back.
	Brahim: Speaking of which, my hand still shakes a little from too much office coffee. Mind helping me trace two beginner talismans before I head back to Tatay's?
	Brahim: First one is the Krus ng Simula—a simple ward to calm a fresh bronze piece.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:1"]
	Brahim: Clean, balanced lines! Even a simple ward hums when it's drawn with care.
	Brahim: Let's try one more—Buwan ni Mayari. Travelers keep this crescent close on dark barangay roads.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:2"]
	Brahim: Mayari's crescent! You've got a steadier hand than I do.
	Brahim: Salamat for the help. I'll also grab {Transaction_ItemWants} for Tatay and me—we're preparing herbs by the creek tonight.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 1:
	Brahim: Your little store has a good rhythm to it. [pause=0.3] Everything right where it belongs.
	Brahim: That old fridge humming in the corner reminds me of my parents' kitchen when I was a kid.
	- It's a little slow, honestly.
		Brahim: Slow isn't a bad thing. In the city, everyone's rushing to beat a deadline nobody remembers the next week.
	- It belonged to my lola.
		Brahim: You can tell. Things that get looked after keep a quiet kind of warmth.
	Brahim: Tatay had me sorting dried sambong and lagundi leaves all morning. My fingers smell like rain and ginger.
	Brahim: I'll take {Transaction_ItemWants}, please. Need something to share with him before our afternoon rounds.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 2:
	Brahim: Tatay had me up past midnight practicing prayers for the household wards.
	Brahim: Back at my old office, staying up late meant fixing someone else's slide deck. Doing it for our neighbors feels completely different.
	- Are you getting the hang of it?
		Brahim: Little by little. Tatay says the words only work if your heart isn't in a hurry.
	- You look much more at ease today.
		Brahim: Karimlan does that to you. The air actually lets you breathe.
	Brahim: I brought two protective charms that need fresh ink before sundown. Mind lending your steady hand again?
	Brahim: First is Mata ng Bantay—the watcher's eye, to keep mischief off a doorstep.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:3"]
	Brahim: You can almost feel it watching back. That'll keep bad luck well away.
	Brahim: And the second—Tala ng Gabay, a guiding star for a fisherman heading out early tomorrow.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:4"]
	Brahim: Sharp points and a steady circle—this charm will never lose its north.
	Brahim: Thanks again. I'll pick up {Transaction_ItemWants} on my way back to Tatay's.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 3:
	Brahim: I passed by the canal earlier and saw some neighborhood kids poking at an anthill, daring each other to say "tabi-tabi po" backwards.
	Brahim: Tatay would've had a fit if he saw them.
	- Did you stop them?
		Brahim: Gently. Told them the old stories instead of scolding them. Kids listen better when you treat them like they're part of the secret.
	- Were they actually scared?
		Brahim: Only until I reminded them how dark that path gets after six. They ran home pretty fast after that.
	Brahim: I promised I'd bring a small peace offering back by the mound later. I'll take {Transaction_ItemWants} for the walk.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 4:
	Brahim: A neighbor down by the river came to Tatay's house with a stubborn fever this morning.
	Brahim: Nothing serious, just exhaustion and a fright from walking home late in the rain. Tatay asked me to prepare two warming charms for her family.
	- That's a lot of trust from your father.
		Brahim: It is. He barely even hovered over my shoulder this time.
	- Need a hand with the brushwork?
		Brahim: I was hoping you'd offer. You have a real knack for this.
	Brahim: Let's start with Tatsulok ng Lunas—the healing triad. The old albularyos always swore by the triangle.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:5"]
	Brahim: Steady and centered. Tatay would be proud of that one.
	Brahim: Now Sinag ng Araw—eight solar rays to bring warmth back to a damp house.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:6"]
	Brahim: Bright as high noon! This one carries real warmth.
	Brahim: Salamat. I'll grab {Transaction_ItemWants} as well—always good to bring something to eat when visiting a recovering neighbor.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 5:
	Brahim: Funny thing happened today. An old coworker from Manila messaged me, asking if I regretted walking away from the promotion.
	Brahim: I looked out the window at the bamboo swaying in the breeze and didn't even know how to explain it to him.
	- What did you tell him?
		Brahim: That I traded a corner desk for a quiet porch, and I'd make the same trade twice.
	- You belong here in Karimlan.
		Brahim: It's starting to feel that way. Even the stray dogs know my footsteps now.
	Brahim: Tatay's resting his knees today, so I'm doing the errands. Just {Transaction_ItemWants} for me, please.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 6:
	Brahim: The wind's been picking up since dawn. Tatay says the mountain air gets restless before a heavy storm.
	Brahim: He asked me to prepare two stronger wards for the barangay chapel and the bridge.
	- Those sound trickier than the early ones.
		Brahim: They are—more intersecting lines, less room for error. Good thing I've got you as my co-inscriber.
	- Ready when you are.
		Brahim: Appreciate it. First up is Kalasag ng Hangin—the wind shield.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:7"]
	Brahim: Solid as narra wood, light as the breeze. No storm's getting past that.
	Brahim: Next is Selyo ng Bituin—twin opposing triangles bound by a sacred ring. Take your time with the intersections.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:8"]
	Brahim: Not a single tremor in those intersections—you really have an albularyo's hand!
	Brahim: I'll take {Transaction_ItemWants} for Tatay too. He's been craving a snack all afternoon.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 7:
	Brahim: I handled my first house call completely on my own today. [pause=0.3] Down at the south end of the barangay.
	Brahim: A family couldn't sleep because of rattling eaves and cold drafts. Turned out to be half loose tin roof, half an old restless spirit looking for quiet.
	- How did you handle it?
		Brahim: Nailed down the loose sheet first, then lit a little kamangyan and spoke the calming prayer Tatay taught me. Both worked together.
	- Tatay must be thrilled.
		Brahim: He didn't say much—just poured me a cup of barako and smiled. That's high praise from him.
	Brahim: I'll grab {Transaction_ItemWants} to celebrate a quiet evening.
	[end_timeline]

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 8:
	Brahim: Tatay handed me his old brass bell this morning. [pause=0.4] Said his hands are ready to rest, and mine are ready to carry the work.
	Brahim: Leaving the corporate world felt terrifying a year ago. Now I can't imagine being anywhere else than right here in Karimlan.
	- Congratulations, Brahim. You earned it.
		Brahim: I couldn't have gotten here without Tatay's patience—and honestly, without stopping by your store whenever I needed a breather.
	- Your father must be so proud.
		Brahim: He pretended he had dust in his eyes. I let him have that one.
	Brahim: For my first official set as Karimlan's new albularyo, I'd be honored if you helped me inscribe two master charms.
	Brahim: First is Orasyon ng Balete—the seal of the rooted tree.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:9"]
	Brahim: Whoa... the air around the counter actually went quiet. That's the real deal.
	Brahim: And the last one—Dakilang Anting-Anting. The grand agimat.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:10"]
	Brahim: A masterwork agimat! I couldn't have inscribed this half as well on my own.
	Brahim: Thank you for everything, friend. I'll take {Transaction_ItemWants}—Tatay and I are having a proper dinner tonight.
	[end_timeline]

label Talk
Brahim: No rush at all—I'm just waiting on {Transaction_ItemWants}.
- On it.
	Brahim: Salamat. Take your time.
	[end_timeline]
- Sorry, we're out.
	Brahim: No worries at all. I'll drop by again once you've restocked.
	[signal arg="refuse_service"]
	[signal arg="story_success"]
	[end_timeline]

label Partial
Brahim: Got that one, salamat. [pause=0.3] I'm still looking for [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] whenever you're ready.
[end_timeline]

label Satisfy
Brahim: Perfect, just what I needed. Salamat!
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label WrongItem
Brahim: Ah, I think that's not quite what I asked for.
Brahim: I was looking for {Transaction_ItemWants}, if you still have it.
[end_timeline]
